Chapter: Zstd
  cites Compress chapter Deflate

 Zstandard (RFC 8878). Raw blocks, RLE blocks, and compressed blocks whose
 literals are Huffman-coded (direct weights, a single backward-read stream, zero
 sequences). Real zstd decodes every block type -- proved by the python-zstandard
 oracle in build/zstd-interop-test.ps1, which is the only thing that can, because
 a round-trip through our own decoder cannot see a bug both halves share. The
 format details, and the frame-header trap that shipped green for months, are in
 docs/Reference/ZstdHuffmanFormat.md.

 The Huffman machinery is Deflate's: the same optimal code-length build and the
 same least-significant-bit-first BitWriter. Only zstd's own pieces are here --
 its weight encoding, its canonical assignment (which distributes from the
 longest codes, opposite to Deflate), and its backward-read bitstream.

 The compressed block is scoped to what direct weights and a single stream allow:
 a literal region of at most 1023 bytes, over an alphabet whose highest byte is
 at most 128 (so the weight header fits one byte), with a code no longer than 11
 bits. Outside those, or when Huffman does not beat a raw block, the region falls
 back to a raw block, so the output never inflates. FSE literals, sequences (real
 LZ matches), and the multi-stream layouts that lift these limits are future work.

 To zstd-compress gives a Zstd-framed byte stream.
 To zstd-decompress gives original bytes from a Zstd stream.
 To zstd-valid gives True when input has a valid Zstd magic number.

 We say:

Section: Constants

  zstd-magic-0 : Integer = 40
  zstd-magic-1 : Integer = 181
  zstd-magic-2 : Integer = 47
  zstd-magic-3 : Integer = 253
  zstd-block-max : Integer = 131071
  zstd-rle-min : Integer = 4
  zstd-lit-max : Integer = 1023
  zstd-max-huf-bits : Integer = 11

Section: Compression (RLE + Compressed + Raw Blocks)

 A run of zstd-rle-min or more identical bytes becomes an RLE block
 (Block_Type 01). A literal region (no long run) is handed to zstd-try-compress:
 if a Huffman-coded compressed block (Block_Type 10) is smaller than a raw block
 it wins, otherwise the region stays a raw block. All three are valid RFC 8878.
 Literal regions are cut at zstd-lit-max so each fits a single-stream compressed
 block's ten-bit Regenerated_Size.

  zstd-compress : List Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-compress (input) =
    let len = list-length input
    in zstd-frame-header len & zstd-emit-blocks input len 0

 The frame header is a single-segment, no-dictionary frame with a FOUR-byte
 Frame_Content_Size (Frame_Header_Descriptor 160 = 0xA0). The two-byte FCS width
 is a trap: RFC 8878 3.1.1.1.4 adds 256 to the stored two-byte value, so a header
 that writes the size directly decodes 256 bytes too large and a real zstd
 decoder rejects the whole frame as corrupt. The four-byte width carries no such
 offset. This chapter shipped the two-byte header for a while and it was never
 real-zstd-valid until a python-zstandard oracle caught it.

  zstd-frame-header : Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-frame-header (content-size) =
    let fhd = 160
    in [zstd-magic-0, zstd-magic-1, zstd-magic-2, zstd-magic-3, fhd,
        bit-and content-size 255, bit-and (bit-shru content-size 8) 255,
        bit-and (bit-shru content-size 16) 255, bit-and (bit-shru content-size 24) 255]

  zstd-emit-blocks : List Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-emit-blocks (input) (total) (pos) =
    if pos >= total then []
    else let b = list-at input pos
    in let run = zstd-run-length input total pos b 0
    in if run >= zstd-rle-min then zstd-emit-rle input total pos b run
    else zstd-emit-literal input total pos

  zstd-emit-rle : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-emit-rle (input) (total) (pos) (b) (run) =
    let chunk = if run > zstd-block-max then zstd-block-max else run
    in let is-last = pos + chunk >= total
    in zstd-rle-block-header is-last chunk & [b] & zstd-emit-blocks input total (pos + chunk)

  zstd-emit-literal : List Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-emit-literal (input) (total) (pos) =
    let lend = zstd-literal-end input total pos
    in let capped = if lend - pos > zstd-lit-max then pos + zstd-lit-max else lend
    in let size = capped - pos
    in let is-last = capped >= total
    in let region = zstd-slice input pos size 0 []
    in let comp = zstd-try-compress region size is-last
    in if list-length comp == 0
      then zstd-raw-block-header is-last size & region & zstd-emit-blocks input total capped
      else comp & zstd-emit-blocks input total capped

  zstd-run-length : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  zstd-run-length (input) (total) (pos) (b) (n) =
    if pos + n >= total then n
    else if list-at input (pos + n) == b then zstd-run-length input total pos b (n + 1)
    else n

  zstd-literal-end : List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  zstd-literal-end (input) (total) (i) =
    if i >= total then i
    else let r = zstd-run-length input total i (list-at input i) 0
    in if r >= zstd-rle-min then i
    else zstd-literal-end input total (i + r)

  zstd-raw-block-header : Boolean, Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-raw-block-header (is-last) (size) =
    let last-bit = if is-last then 1 else 0
    in let raw = bit-or last-bit (bit-shl size 3)
    in [bit-and raw 255, bit-and (bit-shru raw 8) 255, bit-and (bit-shru raw 16) 255]

  zstd-rle-block-header : Boolean, Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-rle-block-header (is-last) (size) =
    let last-bit = if is-last then 1 else 0
    in let raw = bit-or (bit-or last-bit 2) (bit-shl size 3)
    in [bit-and raw 255, bit-and (bit-shru raw 8) 255, bit-and (bit-shru raw 16) 255]

Section: Compressed Literals -- Huffman

 A compressed block here is a Compressed_Literals_Block (Huffman, direct weights,
 one backward-read stream) followed by a Sequences_Section of a single zero byte
 (no matches). The code lengths come from Deflate's optimal Huffman build; the
 weights, the canonical codes and the stream are zstd's own. See
 docs/Reference/ZstdHuffmanFormat.md.

 zstd-try-compress returns the whole block, or the empty list to mean "use a raw
 block instead" -- when the region is too small, its alphabet reaches past 128,
 a code would exceed eleven bits, or Huffman simply does not beat raw.

  zstd-histo : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-histo (xs) (i) (n) (freq) =
    if i >= n then freq
    else let b = list-at xs i
    in zstd-histo xs (i + 1) n (list-set-at freq b (list-at freq b + 1))

  zstd-max-byte : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  zstd-max-byte (xs) (i) (n) (best) =
    if i >= n then best
    else let b = list-at xs i
    in zstd-max-byte xs (i + 1) n (if b > best then b else best)

 Weight = Max_Number_of_Bits + 1 - Number_of_Bits for a present symbol, 0 for an
 absent one. Max_Number_of_Bits is the longest code.

  zstd-weights : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-weights (lengths) (i) (nsym) (maxbits) (acc) =
    if i >= nsym then acc
    else let l = list-at lengths i
    in zstd-weights lengths (i + 1) nsym maxbits (list-push acc (if l > 0 then maxbits + 1 - l else 0))

 Direct weights: two per byte, high nibble first, and the last symbol's weight is
 not written (the decoder completes it to the next power of two).

  zstd-pack-weights : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-pack-weights (weights) (i) (nw) (acc) =
    if i >= nw then acc
    else let hi = list-at weights i
    in let lo = if i + 1 < nw then list-at weights (i + 1) else 0
    in zstd-pack-weights weights (i + 2) nw (list-push acc (bit-or (bit-shl hi 4) lo))

 Canonical codes, zstd order: distribute from the longest code (lowest weight)
 up. The per-length starting codes run the recurrence backward from the top
 length -- start[b] = (start[b+1] + count[b+1]) >> 1 -- then Deflate's assignment
 hands them out in symbol order.

  zstd-start-codes : List Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-start-codes (bl) (maxbits) =
    zstd-start-loop bl maxbits (maxbits - 1) (dh-zeros (maxbits + 1) 0 [])

  zstd-start-loop : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-start-loop (bl) (maxbits) (b) (acc) =
    if b < 1 then acc
    else let sc = bit-shru (list-at acc (b + 1) + list-at bl (b + 1)) 1
    in zstd-start-loop bl maxbits (b - 1) (list-set-at acc b sc)

  zstd-canon-codes : List Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-canon-codes (lengths) (nsym) (maxbits) =
    let bl = dh-bl-count lengths nsym
    in dh-assign-codes lengths 0 nsym (zstd-start-codes bl maxbits) (dh-zeros nsym 0 [])

 The stream is written LSB-first in REVERSE literal order, then a sentinel one
 bit, then padded -- which is exactly Deflate's BitWriter and lays the bytes down
 little-endian so a real zstd decoder reads them backward. (The why is in the
 reference doc.)

  zstd-huf-stream : List Integer, Integer, List Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-huf-stream (region) (size) (codes) (lengths) =
    bw-finish (bw-bits (zstd-huf-loop region (size - 1) codes lengths bw-empty) 1 1)

  zstd-huf-loop : List Integer, Integer, List Integer, List Integer, BitWriter -> BitWriter
  zstd-huf-loop (region) (i) (codes) (lengths) (w) =
    if i < 0 then w
    else let sym = list-at region i
    in zstd-huf-loop region (i - 1) codes lengths (bw-bits w (list-at codes sym) (list-at lengths sym))

  zstd-lit-header : Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-lit-header (regen) (comp) =
    let v = bit-or (bit-or 2 (bit-shl regen 4)) (bit-shl comp 14)
    in [bit-and v 255, bit-and (bit-shru v 8) 255, bit-and (bit-shru v 16) 255]

  zstd-comp-block-header : Boolean, Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-comp-block-header (is-last) (size) =
    let last-bit = if is-last then 1 else 0
    in let raw = bit-or (bit-or last-bit 4) (bit-shl size 3)
    in [bit-and raw 255, bit-and (bit-shru raw 8) 255, bit-and (bit-shru raw 16) 255]

  zstd-try-compress : List Integer, Integer, Boolean -> List Integer
  zstd-try-compress (region) (size) (is-last) =
    if size < 8 then []
    else let max-sym = zstd-max-byte region 0 size 0
    in if max-sym > 128 then []
    else let nsym = max-sym + 1
    in let freq = zstd-histo region 0 size (dh-zeros nsym 0 [])
    in let lengths = dh-lengths-from-freq freq nsym
    in let maxbits = dh-max-len lengths 0 nsym 0
    in if maxbits > zstd-max-huf-bits then []
    else if maxbits < 1 then []
    else let weights = zstd-weights lengths 0 nsym maxbits []
    in let codes = zstd-canon-codes lengths nsym maxbits
    in let tree-desc = [127 + max-sym] & zstd-pack-weights weights 0 max-sym []
    in let stream = zstd-huf-stream region size codes lengths
    in let lit-content = tree-desc & stream
    in let comp-size = list-length lit-content
    in if comp-size > zstd-lit-max then []
    else if comp-size + 4 >= size then []
    else let block-content = zstd-lit-header size comp-size & lit-content & [0]
    in zstd-comp-block-header is-last (list-length block-content) & block-content

 Decoding a compressed block: read the literals header, rebuild the Huffman table
 from the weights (completing the implied last one), then walk the backward
 stream through a max-bits-wide lookup table for exactly Regenerated_Size symbols.
 The single trailing zero byte is the empty Sequences_Section.

  zstd-read-weights : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-read-weights (input) (off) (nw) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= nw then acc
    else let byte = list-at input (off + i / 2)
    in let w = if i - (i / 2) * 2 == 0 then bit-shru byte 4 else bit-and byte 15
    in zstd-read-weights input off nw (i + 1) (list-push acc w)

  zstd-weight-sum : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  zstd-weight-sum (weights) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else let w = list-at weights i
    in zstd-weight-sum weights (i + 1) n (if w > 0 then acc + bit-shl 1 (w - 1) else acc)

  zstd-nextpow2-log : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  zstd-nextpow2-log (partial) (b) =
    if bit-shl 1 b > partial then b else zstd-nextpow2-log partial (b + 1)

  zstd-log2 : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  zstd-log2 (v) (b) =
    if bit-shl 1 b >= v then b else zstd-log2 v (b + 1)

  zstd-nbbits : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-nbbits (weights) (i) (n) (maxbits) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else let w = list-at weights i
    in zstd-nbbits weights (i + 1) n maxbits (list-push acc (if w > 0 then maxbits + 1 - w else 0))

  zstd-highest-bit : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  zstd-highest-bit (byte) (b) =
    if b < 0 then 0 - 1
    else if bit-and (bit-shru byte b) 1 == 1 then b
    else zstd-highest-bit byte (b - 1)

  zstd-byte-bits-down : Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-byte-bits-down (byte) (b) (acc) =
    if b < 0 then acc
    else zstd-byte-bits-down byte (b - 1) (list-push acc (bit-and (bit-shru byte b) 1))

  zstd-stream-earlier : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-stream-earlier (input) (start) (idx) (acc) =
    if idx < start then acc
    else zstd-stream-earlier input start (idx - 1) (zstd-byte-bits-down (list-at input idx) 7 acc)

  zstd-stream-bits : List Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-stream-bits (input) (start) (slen) =
    let last-byte = list-at input (start + slen - 1)
    in let sp = zstd-highest-bit last-byte 7
    in zstd-stream-earlier input start (start + slen - 2) (zstd-byte-bits-down last-byte (sp - 1) [])

  zstd-peek-bits : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  zstd-peek-bits (bits) (cursor) (n) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else let bit = if cursor + i < list-length bits then list-at bits (cursor + i) else 0
    in zstd-peek-bits bits cursor n (i + 1) (bit-or (bit-shl acc 1) bit)

  zstd-fill-range : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-fill-range (table) (base) (cnt) (i) (val) =
    if i >= cnt then table
    else zstd-fill-range (list-set-at table (base + i) val) base cnt (i + 1) val

  zstd-fill-dtable : List Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-fill-dtable (codes) (nbBits) (s) (nsym) (maxbits) (table) =
    if s >= nsym then table
    else let l = list-at nbBits s
    in if l == 0 then zstd-fill-dtable codes nbBits (s + 1) nsym maxbits table
    else let base = bit-shl (list-at codes s) (maxbits - l)
    in zstd-fill-dtable codes nbBits (s + 1) nsym maxbits (zstd-fill-range table base (bit-shl 1 (maxbits - l)) 0 (s * 16 + l))

  zstd-build-dtable : List Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-build-dtable (codes) (nbBits) (nsym) (maxbits) =
    zstd-fill-dtable codes nbBits 0 nsym maxbits (dh-zeros (bit-shl 1 maxbits) 0 [])

  zstd-huf-decode : List Integer, Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-huf-decode (bits) (cursor) (dtable) (maxbits) (count) (acc) =
    if count <= 0 then acc
    else let entry = list-at dtable (zstd-peek-bits bits cursor maxbits 0 0)
    in let sym = entry / 16
    in zstd-huf-decode bits (cursor + entry - sym * 16) dtable maxbits (count - 1) (list-push acc sym)

  zstd-decode-compressed : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-decode-compressed (input) (pos) (len) (block-size) (is-last) (acc) =
    let cstart = pos + 3
    in let h = bit-or (bit-or (list-at input cstart) (bit-shl (list-at input (cstart + 1)) 8)) (bit-shl (list-at input (cstart + 2)) 16)
    in let regen = bit-and (bit-shru h 4) 1023
    in let comp-size = bit-and (bit-shru h 14) 1023
    in let tree-start = cstart + 3
    in let num-weights = list-at input tree-start - 127
    in let tree-desc-len = 1 + (num-weights + 1) / 2
    in let weights0 = zstd-read-weights input (tree-start + 1) num-weights 0 []
    in let partial = zstd-weight-sum weights0 0 num-weights 0
    in let maxbits = zstd-nextpow2-log partial 0
    in let last-w = 1 + zstd-log2 (bit-shl 1 maxbits - partial) 0
    in let weights = list-push weights0 last-w
    in let nbBits = zstd-nbbits weights 0 (num-weights + 1) maxbits []
    in let codes = zstd-canon-codes nbBits (num-weights + 1) maxbits
    in let dtable = zstd-build-dtable codes nbBits (num-weights + 1) maxbits
    in let bits = zstd-stream-bits input (tree-start + tree-desc-len) (comp-size - tree-desc-len)
    in let acc2 = acc & zstd-huf-decode bits 0 dtable maxbits regen []
    in if is-last == 1 then acc2
    else zstd-decode-blocks input (pos + 3 + block-size) len acc2

Section: Decompression

  zstd-decompress : List Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-decompress (input) =
    if zstd-valid input == False then []
    else zstd-decode-blocks input (zstd-header-len input) (list-length input) []

 The frame header length is read from the Frame_Header_Descriptor (RFC 8878
 3.1.1.1.1): its top two bits pick the Frame_Content_Size field width, bit 5 is
 the Single_Segment flag (a Window_Descriptor byte is present only when it is
 zero), and the low two bits pick the Dictionary_ID width. Our encoder always
 writes a single-segment, no-dictionary, four-byte-FCS header (nine bytes), but
 reading the descriptor keeps the decoder honest rather than assuming its own
 encoder's shape.

  zstd-header-len : List Integer -> Integer
  zstd-header-len (input) =
    let fhd = list-at input 4
    in let fcs-flag = bit-and (bit-shru fhd 6) 3
    in let single = bit-and (bit-shru fhd 5) 1
    in let did-flag = bit-and fhd 3
    in let fcs = if fcs-flag == 0 then (if single == 1 then 1 else 0)
                 else if fcs-flag == 1 then 2
                 else if fcs-flag == 2 then 4
                 else 8
    in let win = if single == 1 then 0 else 1
    in let did = if did-flag == 0 then 0 else if did-flag == 1 then 1 else if did-flag == 2 then 2 else 4
    in 5 + win + did + fcs

  zstd-decode-blocks : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-decode-blocks (input) (pos) (len) (acc) =
    if pos + 2 >= len then acc
    else let header = bit-or (bit-or (list-at input pos) (bit-shl (list-at input (pos + 1)) 8)) (bit-shl (list-at input (pos + 2)) 16)
    in let is-last = bit-and header 1
    in let block-type = bit-and (bit-shru header 1) 3
    in let block-size = bit-shru header 3
    in if block-type == 1 then zstd-decode-rle input pos len block-size is-last acc
    else if block-type == 2 then zstd-decode-compressed input pos len block-size is-last acc
    else zstd-decode-raw input pos len block-size is-last acc

  zstd-decode-raw : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-decode-raw (input) (pos) (len) (block-size) (is-last) (acc) =
    let data = zstd-slice input (pos + 3) block-size 0 []
    in let acc2 = acc & data
    in if is-last == 1 then acc2
    else zstd-decode-blocks input (pos + 3 + block-size) len acc2

  zstd-decode-rle : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-decode-rle (input) (pos) (len) (block-size) (is-last) (acc) =
    let data = zstd-repeat (list-at input (pos + 3)) block-size 0 []
    in let acc2 = acc & data
    in if is-last == 1 then acc2
    else zstd-decode-blocks input (pos + 3 + 1) len acc2

  zstd-repeat : Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-repeat (b) (count) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= count then acc
    else zstd-repeat b count (i + 1) (list-push acc b)

Section: Validation

  zstd-valid : List Integer -> Boolean
  zstd-valid (input) =
    if list-length input < 7 then False
    else if list-at input 0 == zstd-magic-0 then
      if list-at input 1 == zstd-magic-1 then
        if list-at input 2 == zstd-magic-2 then
          list-at input 3 == zstd-magic-3
        else False
      else False
    else False

Section: Helpers

  zstd-slice : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  zstd-slice (xs) (off) (len) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= len then acc
    else if off + i >= list-length xs then acc
    else zstd-slice xs off len (i + 1) (list-push acc (list-at xs (off + i)))

